OL,3,GNEWSAYour guide to Remembrance events
OL,4,Aacross the South
OL,5,
OL,6,FCommunities in the south of England are
OL,7,Fset to come together to honour the
OL,8,Flives of the armed forces, veterans and
OL,9,Ftheir families in Remembrance services.
OL,11,FPeople across Dorset, Berkshire,
OL,12,FOxfordshire, the Isle of Wight and
OL,13,FHampshire will gather on Sunday 8
OL,14,FNovember and Wednesday 11 November to
OL,15,Fmark Remembrance Sunday and Armistice
OL,16,FDay.
OL,18,FRemembrance Sunday is traditionally the
OL,19,Fsecond Sunday of November each year,
OL,20,Fwhile Armistice Day is always on 11
OL,21,FNovember to mark the moment World War
OL,22,FOne ended.
OL,23,APub: 06-NovQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
